    dict(key='14-act-3-figure', kind='figure', title='Types that print safely',
         body='types_print',
         narration="Third demo: make the secret unprintable. [[slnc 400]] On the left, the input: what the code holds. [[slnc 300]] A name, a Card with the full number, a Secret with the C V V, and the order number. [[slnc 700]] On the right, how each one prints. [[slnc 300]] A Card's to string method gives four stars and the last four digits. [[slnc 300]] A Secret's to string gives redacted. [[slnc 300]] Only reveal gives the value, and only the code that needs it calls it. [[slnc 700]] At the bottom, the result: the log file, through a plain layout, with no masking at all. [[slnc 300]] Nothing to mask, because the secret never reached the line. [[slnc 300]] And the library's exception is logged by its class name and a reference, never by its message."),
